\title{LCZ4r: Tools for Local Climate Zones and Urban Heat Island Analysis}
\description{
Tools for analysing and visualising Local Climate Zones (LCZ) and urban heat islands at multiple spatial and temporal resolutions. Provides functions to retrieve LCZ maps from global, European and continental United States datasets and from the 'LCZ Generator', compute LCZ areas and urban canopy parameters, and combine LCZ maps with air temperature observations to analyse time series, thermal anomalies and urban heat island intensity, and to produce and evaluate LCZ-based kriging interpolation maps. Methods follow Stewart and Oke (2012) \doi{10.1175/BAMS-D-11-00019.1} and Demuzere et al. (2022) \doi{10.5194/essd-14-3835-2022}.
}
\section{Example data}{

The file \code{extdata/lcz_berlin.tif} is a small LCZ map of Berlin,
Germany, used in the examples. It was cropped from the European LCZ map of
Demuzere et al. (2019) \doi{10.1371/journal.pone.0214474} (redistributed in
\doi{10.5281/zenodo.10835692}) and reprojected to WGS84. Load it with:
\preformatted{
lcz_map <- terra::rast(system.file("extdata", "lcz_berlin.tif", package = "LCZ4r"))
}
}

